& [BoundaryFormation] separates structural assembly from acquisition
  + [inside] one exact profile, requested entry kind, component, component bound, and five required supplied record classes
  + [inside] correlation equality, cross-field coherence, stream revalidation, pure entry-policy evaluation, and explicit projection
  + [outside] query success, buffer initialization, handle ownership, same-handle provenance, physical completeness, freshness, filesystem support, path binding, traversal, Git interpretation, receipts, and effects
  + [required_records] are attribute-tag, file-identity, standard-information, case-sensitivity disposition, and stream-set disposition
  + [presence] is enforced by nonoptional fields and closed variants rather than defaults

& [AtomicRequirementSet] is complete
  + [M2B-SEO-001] bind strict profile, strict JSON, preserved source, governing protocol, and required nonoptional records
  + [M2B-SEO-002] require every supplied record to carry nonzero equal batch and entry-reference identities
  + [M2B-SEO-003] preserve exact attributes and diagnostic reparse tag without turning either into provenance
  + [M2B-SEO-004] require exactly sixteen supplied file-ID bytes and derive only canonical lowercase hexadecimal identity text
  + [M2B-SEO-005] reject negative allocation size or end-of-file length before unsigned conversion
  + [M2B-SEO-006] require nonzero link count and reject every delete-pending record
  + [M2B-SEO-007] require requested kind, standard-information directory flag, and DIRECTORY attribute interpretation to agree
  + [M2B-SEO-008] require directory case flags as an exact flags record for directory and an explicit not-applicable record for regular file
  + [M2B-SEO-009] invoke the current pure entry-policy kernel with exact profile, kind, attributes, case flags, component, and component bound
  + [M2B-SEO-010] require streams as either an explicit empty variant or an ordered-records variant with no completeness boolean
  + [M2B-SEO-011] revalidate stream grammar, exact uniqueness, count and UTF-16 bounds, and strictly increasing source offsets while preserving supplied order and raw sizes
  + [M2B-SEO-012] release one immutable observation or one closed bounded fault with no partial accepted value
  + [M2B-SEO-013] expose only an explicit M2A projection seed that omits path, mode class, content digest, and observation ordinal
  + [M2B-SEO-014] keep correlation and structural coherence explicitly weaker than physical provenance, completeness, or trust
  + [M2B-SEO-015] preserve zero dependencies, zero unsafe, zero platform calls, and zero runtime effects
  + [M2B-SEO-016] bind focused, static, evidence, global, rollback, and downstream stop-gate proof

& [DataDesignModel] is one closed pure transform
  + [RecordCorrelation] is batch_identity u64 plus entry_reference_identity u64
  + [SuppliedAttributeTagRecord] is correlation, exact attributes u32, and diagnostic reparse_tag u32
  + [SuppliedFileIdentityRecord] is correlation, volume_serial u64, and file_id_bytes fixed at sixteen u8 values
  + [SuppliedStandardInformationRecord] is correlation, allocation_size i64, end_of_file i64, number_of_links u32, delete_pending bool, and directory bool
  + [SuppliedCaseSensitivityRecord] is directory_flags with correlation and flags or not_applicable with correlation
  + [SuppliedStreamSet] is explicit_empty with correlation or ordered_records with correlation and raw parser records
  + [AssemblyInput] is profile, kind, component, component bound, and exactly one value of every required record class
  + [SuppliedEntryObservation] preserves the shared correlation, policy decision, diagnostic tag, strong identity, nonnegative sizes, links, and supplied stream order
  + [TopologyProjectionSeed] contains only kind, attributes, strong identity, links, canonical stream facts, and kind-shaped length
  + [AssemblyFault] is one closed code, field, and bounded deterministic reason
  + [lifecycle] is supplied syntax to correlation to coherence to policy to one observation or one fault
  + [state] is absent
  - never: release a partial observation

& [CorrelationTruthTable] is exhaustive
  + [all_nonzero_and_equal] proceeds
  + [any_zero_batch_identity] rejects as correlation fault
  + [any_zero_entry_reference_identity] rejects as correlation fault
  + [any_batch_difference] rejects as correlation fault
  + [any_entry_reference_difference] rejects as correlation fault
  + [meaning] correlation syntax permits equality checks only

& [KindAndCaseTruthTable] is exhaustive
  + [directory] requires standard directory true, DIRECTORY attribute admitted by the entry policy, and directory_flags variant with exact zero flags
  + [regular_file] requires standard directory false, no DIRECTORY attribute admitted by the entry policy, and explicit not_applicable case variant
  + [all_other_combinations] reject before observation release
  + [delete_pending_true] always rejects
  + [number_of_links_zero] always rejects
  + [negative_size] always rejects before conversion

& [StreamTruthTable] is exact
  + [explicit_empty] releases an empty raw stream vector and makes no physical-enumeration claim
  + [ordered_records] requires one through 1024 records
  + [name] is exact default grammar ::$DATA or exact nonempty named grammar :name:$DATA with no inner colon or NUL
  + [name_bound] is one through 32767 UTF-16 code units
  + [uniqueness] is exact String equality across the collection
  + [order] preserves supplied record order and requires source_offset to increase strictly
  + [raw_facts] preserve stream_size, allocation_size, and source_offset
  + [projection] clones and sorts only derived TopologyStreamFact values by exact name for M2A shape compatibility
  - never: infer that Windows returned the collection or that enumeration was complete

& [ProjectionDelineation] prevents invented M2A facts
  + [derived] regular-file length is supplied end_of_file and directory length is absent
  + [derived] parser default name maps to unnamed_default and every admitted named DATA stream maps to named_data
  + [derived] strong identity hex is exact lowercase encoding of sixteen supplied bytes
  + [omitted] relative_path
  + [omitted] mode_class
  + [omitted] content_sha256
  + [omitted] observation_ordinal
  + [not_constructed] TopologyEntryObservation
  - never: implement From or Into that silently fills an omitted field

& [ConstraintLedger] is fail closed
  + [C-01] source and manifest remain byte-bound and separate from derived artifacts
  + [C-02] profile is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-entry-observation/0.1
  + [C-03] all five required records are nonoptional
  + [C-04] no input field is named same_handle, query_succeeded, fully_initialized, trusted, or complete
  + [C-05] correlation identities are nonzero and equal across every record
  + [C-06] fixed file identity is exactly sixteen bytes
  + [C-07] signed sizes reject before unsigned conversion, links reject at zero, and delete pending always rejects
  + [C-08] kind, directory flag, case variant, and entry-policy result agree
  + [C-09] raw stream records are independently revalidated because public structs can be constructed without the parser
  + [C-10] stream order is preserved in the raw observation and projection sorting occurs only in a distinct derived value
  + [C-11] faults contain no partial observation
  + [C-12] M2A projection cannot represent unsupplied path, Git mode, digest, or ordinal
  + [C-13] production imports remain std, serde, and existing pure crate modules
  + [C-14] Cargo, lockfile, unsafe, platform, filesystem, process, environment, clock, network, persistence, model, and effect deltas remain zero
  + [C-15] current entry-policy and stream-parser authority must remain valid
  + [C-16] no evidence language upgrades syntax or coherence into physical proof

& [SubcomponentWeaveTrace] is source grounded
  + [correlation] originates in SuppliedRecordIntent and weaves through every record and fault-path test
  + [identity] originates in file_identity and weaves to fixed-array decoding and strong-identity projection
  + [standard] originates in standard and weaves to signed size, link, delete-pending, and kind tests
  + [case] originates in conditional case intent and weaves to a closed explicit variant
  + [streams] originate in parsed collection intent and weave to independent grammar, bound, uniqueness, order, and preservation tests
  + [policy] originates in CoherenceIntent and weaves to the exact existing evaluator
  + [projection] originates in the anti-invention clause and weaves to a deliberately incomplete seed type

& [CrossWeaveTrace] joins existing fabric
  + [entry_policy] supplies exact kind, attribute, case, component, and order decision
  + [stream_parser] supplies the raw record vocabulary but no physical-completeness claim
  + [topology_forms] supplies strong identity, stream fact, stream kind, and entry kind projection vocabularies
